      "currency": "USD",
      "description": "ForzaTune Pro is a fast, flexible Forza tuning calculator for road, track, drift, rally, and more. Make your own tunes for Forza Horizon 6 (FH6), FH5, Forza Motorsport and earlier Forza games. ForzaTune's streamlined UI keeps the process to about 55 seconds.\n\nThis Forza tuning app uses your build details and what you want the car to do to calculate a complete setup. Simple controls then help you fine-tune the handling.\n\nSTART WITH YOUR EXACT BUILD\n\nChoose from a database of more than 1,550 vehicles and enter a few details about your setup. The tuning formulas account for your vehicle, upgrades, and suspension type.\n\nTUNE FOR ROAD, TRACK, DRIFT, RALLY & MORE\n\nSet up cars for track, balanced road driving, highway runs, touge, time attack, drifting, drag racing, rally or off-road use. Select the tune type that fits what you are building and where you plan to drive it.\n\nTAKE CONTROL OF HANDLING & FEEL\n\nThis is your tune. Adjust overall balance, turn entry, turn exit, ride stiffness and roll stiffness. ForzaTune updates the related settings together so you can customize the handling for your driving style.\n\nIMPROVE ACCELERATION, MID-RANGE PULL & SPEED\n\nDoes your new build include power upgrades? Use the gearing calculator to build ratios around the engine's new power band. ForzaTune's \"triple-stage\" gearing formulas balance acceleration, mid-range pull and top speed.\n\nEASILY UPDATE OR CHANGE TUNES\n\nSave tunes for later and keep updating them as your build changes. Search, edit, export and import tools make it easy to revisit setups.\n\nONE APP TO TUNE THEM ALL\n\nForzaTune Pro supports Forza Horizon 6 (FH6), Forza Horizon 5, Forza Horizon 4, Forza Motorsport (2023), Forza Motorsport 7 and earlier supported titles. More than 1,550 vehicles are included across supported games.\n\nREAL TUNING IDEAS PLUS FORZA EXPERIENCE\n\nForzaTune Pro combines real-world tuning ideas with proven Forza tuning strategies. Get complete settings for suspension, alignment, aero, braking, differential and gearing. Explore setups beyond typical meta tuning.\n\nBUILT WITH THE FORZA COMMUNITY\n\nForzaTune has grown through feedback from thousands of players. It is developed by Anthony Curtis, an engineer and Forza player since 2005.\n\n\nFAQs\n-----\n\nIs this for beginners or experienced tuners?\nBoth. Experienced tuners use it to save time and typically run higher oversteer settings. Newer tuners use it to learn how to tune and make sure the cars are stable after upgrading.\n\nWhat upgrades or settings do I need?\nYou will need race, drift, rally or other adjustable suspension types, along with upgrades such as anti-roll bars and differentials. Brakes and aero upgrades are optional. Be sure to disable STM (stability control) and use normal/simulation steering for best results.\n\nIs ForzaTune Pro a subscription?\nNo, ForzaTune Pro is a one-time purchase and works without an account. New cars and features are included at no additional cost. ForzaTune apps have been maintained since 2009, with over 100 free content updates in the modern Forza era.\n\n---\nMake your own tunes, faster with ForzaTune Pro.",
